#!/bin/sh
# screenshot screen|region|window|edit
#   screen  the focused monitor     region  a selected area
#   window  the focused window      edit    a selected area, opened in swappy
# Saves to ~/Pictures/Screenshots and copies the image to the clipboard.
set -eu
dir="${XDG_PICTURES_DIR:-$HOME/Pictures}/Screenshots"
file="$dir/$(date +%Y-%m-%d_%H-%M-%S).png"
mkdir -p "$dir"

case "${1:-}" in
	screen)
		out="$(swaymsg -t get_outputs | jq -r '.[] | select(.focused) | .name')"
		grim -o "$out" "$file" ;;
	region)
		geo="$(slurp)" || exit 0 # Escape cancels the selection
		grim -g "$geo" "$file" ;;
	window)
		geo="$(swaymsg -t get_tree | jq -r '.. | select(.focused? == true) | .rect | "\(.x),\(.y) \(.width)x\(.height)"')"
		grim -g "$geo" "$file" ;;
	edit)
		geo="$(slurp)" || exit 0
		grim -g "$geo" - | swappy -f - -o "$file"
		exit 0 ;;
	*) echo "usage: screenshot screen|region|window|edit" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac

wl-copy --type image/png <"$file"
notify-send -a screenshot -i "$file" "Screenshot saved" "${file#"$HOME"/} (copied to clipboard)"
